enonce.fr:
Peut-on obtenir le polynôme $h(x) = x$ à partir des polynômes $f(x)$ et $g(x)$ par les opérations \textbf{addition, soustraction, multiplication} si

(a) $f(x) = x^2 + x$, $g(x) = x^2 + 2$ ; (b) $f(x) = 2x^2 + x$, $g(x) = 2x$ ;

(c) $f(x) = x^2 + x$, $g(x) = x^2 - 2$ ?

enonce.en:
Can you get the polynomial $h(x) = x$ from the polynomials $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ by the operations \textbf{addition, subtraction, multiplication} if

(a) $f(x) = x^2 + x$, $g(x) = x^2 + 2$; (b) $f(x) = 2x^2 + x$, $g(x) = 2x$;

(c) $f(x) = x^2 + x$, $g(x) = x^2 - 2$?

